"message": "The clinician attributes the patient's 9 kg weight gain to DTG and is considering switching away from DTG. However, the patient has classic hypothyroidism signs (tiredness, cold intolerance, constipation, dry skin, periorbital puffiness, delayed reflexes) with TSH 12.4 mIU/L and low Free T4. She reports often forgetting her levothyroxine. Untreated hypothyroidism is a well-recognized cause of significant weight gain and could fully account for the 9 kg increase. Switching from DTG without first correcting the hypothyroidism may not resolve the weight issue and risks losing the benefits of a well-tolerated, high-genetic-barrier regimen with viral suppression.",
"recommended_action": "Optimise levothyroxine adherence and dose to normalise TSH before attributing weight gain to DTG or switching ART. Reassess weight after thyroid control is achieved.",
